-- title:
--   Sections of 𝒪(mε) non-vanishing along ε
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian local ring, let $C$ be a scheme over $\operatorname{Spec} R$ via a morphism $c$ that is proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, and let $\varepsilon$ be a section of $c$, i.e. a pair consisting of a morphism $\varepsilon_1 : \operatorname{Spec} R \to C$ together with the identity $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $c$ equals the identity of $\operatorname{Spec} R$. Assume furthermore given a two-chart affine cover $\mathcal V$ of $C$: two opens $U_0, U_1$, each affine, with affine intersection and $U_0 \sqcup U_1 = \top$. The assertion is that there exists $m_1 \in \mathbb N$ such that for every $m \ge m_1$ there is a morphism $s$ of $\mathcal O_C$-modules from the unit object $\mathbf 1$ of the monoidal category of modules on $C$ to the dual $(ihom)$ of the module attached to the $m$-th power of the kernel ideal sheaf $\mathcal I_\varepsilon = \varepsilon_1.\mathrm{ker}$ — that is, a global section of $\mathcal O(m\varepsilon) = (\mathcal I_\varepsilon^m)^{\vee}$, where the module of an ideal sheaf datum $I$ is the kernel of the unit-to-pushforward-unit map of the associated closed immersion — such that no point in the image of the underlying map of topological spaces of $\varepsilon_1$ lies in the support of the zero-scheme ideal sheaf of $s$, the latter being the infimum of those ideal sheaf data $J$ on $C$ for which, on every affine open $U$, the ideal generated by the coefficients of $s$ over $U$ is contained in $J$ on $U$.
--
--   This is the existence of a section of $\mathcal O(m\varepsilon)$, for all sufficiently large $m$, having a pole of exact order $m$ along the given section $\varepsilon$, obtained from Riemann–Roch on geometric fibres together with surjectivity of base change in degree zero; the bound can be taken to be twice the fibral genus. It feeds the construction of two-chart pole data on $C$ used to produce Weierstrass-type coordinates for the relative curve.
